# Biome 1, level 1 — First Waters
#
# The tutorial shape: a spring on the western rim, a hub five cells east, and a
# straight run between them. Clearing the target needs one route of four
# conduits, which is also the Pivot Token threshold, so a player who finishes
# the level earns their first token by doing so.
#
# Edge directions run clockwise on screen from due east: 0 east, 1 south-east,
# 2 south-west, 3 west, 4 north-west, 5 north-east. Opposite edges are always
# three apart. Clockwise is what HexMetrics guarantees by negating the vertical
# axis, so a turn in the simulation and a turn on screen agree.

id: biome1-01
name: First Waters

base-score: 100
target-score: 246

tokens: 0

# Three skips, so an awkward opening draw is not a dead end before any route exists.
skips: 3

shape: hexagon 3

spring: -3,0 water
hub: 2,0 water

# Mostly straights, with bends so the board is not a single forced line.
tile: 0,3 water x6
tile: 0,2 water x3
